From: =?utf-8?b?T25kxZllaiBTdXLDvQ==?= <ondrej@sury.org>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:06:55 +0100
Subject: Make the openssl tests work with OpenSSL security level 2

OpenSSL runs at security level 2 in Debian, which refuses the
pre-generated test certificates with 1024-bit keys and the TLS versions
older than 1.2. Backport of upstream commits 6b702eea15e, dd7d161ccf1,
58ca47aff64, 72b3987c2d5, 8ba0624a09f (PHP 7.4.8) and 703bbf52105
(PHP 7.4.18), which generate the certificates in the tests and lower the
security level where TLS 1.0 and 1.1 are tested.
